  "name": "Nurthi (Sinhala stage-musical song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song of the Sinhala musical stage drama that grew up in Colombo from the late nineteenth century under the influence of touring Parsi theatre companies from Bombay, setting Sinhala lyrics to North Indian raga-based stage melodies. The productions of John de Silva, staged at the Tower Hall theatre, and the plays of Charles Dias made it the leading popular entertainment of the early twentieth century, and nurthi songs were issued on gramophone 78s with harmonium and tabla accompaniment.",
